## 🧠 Vulnerability Description
Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) is a vulnerability that allows an attacker to inject malicious scripts into a web application. These scripts execute in the victim's browser and can steal session cookies, redirect users, or perform actions on behalf of the victim.

